WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.170 --> 00:00:06.470
Law went to save Luffy at Marineford, not
because he's such a nice guy, but because

00:00:06.470 --> 00:00:13.240
he knew Luffy was a D. He was actually incredible
disappointed when Luffy beat Doflamingo. And

00:00:13.240 --> 00:00:20.170
his name, Trafalgar D. Water Law holds the
key to the shockingly important role Law still

00:00:20.170 --> 00:00:26.310
has to play in the story. If just like me,
you've also always struggled to fully understand

00:00:26.310 --> 00:00:31.340
Law's thoughts and objectives and why the
hell he still sticks around, even after taking

00:00:31.340 --> 00:00:37.280
down his sworn enemy, today I will unravel
everything you want to know about his character

00:00:37.280 --> 00:00:46.780
for you.

00:00:46.780 --> 00:00:51.100
The thing that intrigued me the most about
Trafalgar D. Water Law, when he was introduced

00:00:51.100 --> 00:00:57.039
early on in the story, was how hard is was
to read his thoughts and actions. On Sabaody,

00:00:57.039 --> 00:01:02.069
we meet him as this pretty messed up guy in
hippy clothes, that has fun tormenting his

00:01:02.069 --> 00:01:07.321
enemies, always with a smirk on his face,
which I found immediately intriguing. After

00:01:07.321 --> 00:01:13.170
the war, and especially after the time skip
however, I was surprised to see that he seemingly

00:01:13.170 --> 00:01:18.640
had completely lost this chaotic side of him
and now felt a lot more serious, always thinking

00:01:18.640 --> 00:01:23.420
things through and worrying about things that
might go wrong. Finally, after dethroning

00:01:23.420 --> 00:01:28.540
Doflamingo, it was really heartwarming for
me to him grow closer and closer with the

00:01:28.540 --> 00:01:34.490
straw hats, slowly dropping his serious and
tense manner and fully subscribing to Luffy's

00:01:34.490 --> 00:01:43.390
way of handling things. [We're gonna beat
your ass. What he said, chapter 758, not sure

00:01:43.390 --> 00:01:44.390
what episode]

00:01:44.390 --> 00:01:48.700
Now, what appears to be an inconsistency with
his character, turned out to be one of the

00:01:48.700 --> 00:01:53.210
best character arcs we have gotten in the
story. Law's backstory and his personal history

00:01:53.210 --> 00:01:59.149
with Doflamingo and Corazon is one of my all-time
favorite flashbacks, that I actually dedicated

00:01:59.149 --> 00:02:05.479
a whole video to. It's structured just like
the backstories of all the straw hats, death,

00:02:05.479 --> 00:02:10.860
tragedy and something that Luffy has to free
them from. In the case of Law, that thing

00:02:10.860 --> 00:02:16.810
is his obsession with Doflamingo. After being
saved and loved by Corazon, who tells him

00:02:16.810 --> 00:02:21.760
about the will of D., Law believes that he
must inherit his saviors will to take down

00:02:21.760 --> 00:02:31.730
Doflamingo and for the threat he poses to
the world. I think something that is quite

00:02:31.730 --> 00:02:36.750
easy to overlook, is that Law believes that
Corazon saved him because he revealed his

00:02:36.750 --> 00:02:42.730
middle name to him. Thus he tries to pay this
kindness back by dedicating his whole life

00:02:42.730 --> 00:02:43.730
to revenge.

00:02:43.730 --> 00:02:49.209
This obsession is further fueled, because
Law blames himself for the death of his loved

00:02:49.209 --> 00:02:54.400
ones. He believes himself to be a failure,
which might sound weird to western fans, who

00:02:54.400 --> 00:02:58.659
I think generally see Law as a pretty damn
accomplished character. However, what living

00:02:58.659 --> 00:03:04.110
in Japan has taught me, is that the strong
theme of brothers in Dressrosa, is not by

00:03:04.110 --> 00:03:09.000
accident. We have this for Luffy and Sabo,
who reunite over their shared goal to retrieve

00:03:09.000 --> 00:03:21.579
Ace's devil fruit. But for Law it is particularly
important. See, here in Japan, the relationship

00:03:21.579 --> 00:03:28.700
between older and younger sibling is somewhat
sacred. You should respect your older brother,

00:03:28.700 --> 00:03:34.540
but it is always his duty to protect his younger
siblings. Which is for instance why Ace's

00:03:34.540 --> 00:03:40.410
death was extremely meaningful. Law however,
despite training to be a doctor, is unable

00:03:40.410 --> 00:03:45.159
to save his little sister, and we get this
heartbreaking scene where he has the same

00:03:45.159 --> 00:03:55.200
reaction as Luffy when she dies. Similarly
he can't protect the other orphans. And I

00:03:55.200 --> 00:04:00.540
would even go so far as to say that he blames
himself for Corazon's death as well. See,

00:04:00.540 --> 00:04:07.769
it never occurred to Law, nor to any Japanese
reader, that Doflamingo would do the unthinkable

00:04:07.769 --> 00:04:14.939
and kill his younger sibling. And law as an
older brother, once again had to loose a younger

00:04:14.939 --> 00:04:26.580
sibling he loved. I hope that helps you realize,
why Dressrosa was even more impactful to eastern

00:04:26.580 --> 00:04:32.730
fans than it already was. And why Law is even
more popular among fans there.

00:04:32.730 --> 00:04:38.120
Now of course Law, as a helpless and traumatized
boy is not to blame for any of these, but

00:04:38.120 --> 00:04:42.750
it didn't change the fact that he always felt
guilty about it. In laws mind, taking down

00:04:42.750 --> 00:04:48.430
Doflamingo and fulfilling Corazon's mission,
is the only way to remedy himself from this

00:04:48.430 --> 00:04:54.080
guilt. So up until Sabaody, just like Luffy
and the other supernova, he is mostly focusing

00:04:54.080 --> 00:04:58.430
on getting stronger and so the Law we meet
at the auction house is simply enjoying how

00:04:58.430 --> 00:05:08.470
much closer he has gotten to Dofi in terms
of strength.

00:05:08.470 --> 00:05:14.130
After the war however, things change. Law
finally realizes that the new era is there

00:05:14.130 --> 00:05:19.700
and with it, his chance to make a move. He
saves Luffy, the person who he saw punching

00:05:19.700 --> 00:05:24.420
a celestial dragon and becoming the center
of attention at marineford, because he sees

00:05:24.420 --> 00:05:29.310
someone else, who is capable of fulfilling
Corazon's hopes for the D clan. So after he

00:05:29.310 --> 00:05:35.020
spends 2 years planning his move on Doflamingo,
he doesn't hesitate to team up with Luffy

00:05:35.020 --> 00:05:46.370
once they cross paths on Punk Hazard, completely
by accident. Law very quickly realizes though,

00:05:46.370 --> 00:05:51.340
that without Luffy, his plan would already
have failed right here on Punk Hazard and

00:05:51.340 --> 00:05:57.590
more and more is taken in by Luffy's ability
to master any situation, no matter how impossible

00:05:57.590 --> 00:05:59.030
it may seem.

00:05:59.030 --> 00:06:03.440
After being taken out by Doffi and having
to leave the fight he was waiting for his

00:06:03.440 --> 00:06:10.400
entire life to Luffy, he even says that in
case Luffy should die, he wanted to die next

00:06:10.400 --> 00:06:21.930
to him. At this point, Law fully trusts and
respects our captain. And yet, when Luffy

00:06:21.930 --> 00:06:29.060
finally defeats Dofi after what feels like
12.473 episodes, when all citizens of Dressrosa

00:06:29.060 --> 00:06:37.520
are swept away by tears of joy and receive,
this is the reaction of Law. At first, I thought

00:06:37.520 --> 00:06:44.410
that Law simply has to process what has happened,
but this is the only reaction we get from

00:06:44.410 --> 00:06:50.840
him. Even though his big goal has been achieved,
he still doesn't feel free and fulfilled.

00:06:50.840 --> 00:06:57.310
The weight is still there. And I think this
is why so many people are confused about Law's

00:06:57.310 --> 00:06:58.310
character arc.

00:06:58.310 --> 00:07:03.440
The TRUE resolution to his past, where he
can finally embrace Luffy's deed and come

00:07:03.440 --> 00:07:07.690
back into the light, is a much smaller moment
during the epilogue of Dressrosa.

