00:07:47.110 --> 00:07:51.940
Then moment I'm talking about is this small
interaction he has with Sengoku, the former

00:07:51.940 --> 00:07:58.210
fleet admiral, who had been Corazon's supervisor
within the Marines. Law tells him, that even

00:07:58.210 --> 00:08:02.560
after they took out Doflamingo, he doesn't
know whether he became the type of D. Corazon

00:08:02.560 --> 00:08:06.940
wanted him to be. What both Sengoku and I
realized in this moment, is the fact that

00:08:06.940 --> 00:08:12.430
Law has always assumed that he had been saved
for being a D. An enemy of the gods, with

00:08:12.430 --> 00:08:17.960
high expectations in him to fulfill his role.
The beautify of this scene is how Sengoku

00:08:17.960 --> 00:08:24.360
breaks Law's world view with one sentence
and frees him form his past. He tells him

00:08:24.360 --> 00:08:32.020
that Corazon never truly new anything about
the D, and that he surely didn't save Law

00:08:32.020 --> 00:08:39.979
because of it. And so it is these two panels
here, that actually mark the conclusion of

00:08:39.979 --> 00:08:44.000
Law's arc and the end of his suffering. Oda's
subtle genius.

00:08:44.000 --> 00:08:49.920
Okay, so Law's arc is over right? He has done
what he set out to do and even found peace

00:08:49.920 --> 00:08:56.269
by embracing the unconditional love Corazon
had for him. So, why exactly is Law still

00:08:56.269 --> 00:09:01.910
there? What is his purpose in the story and
what goal does he have now? Two common theories

00:09:01.910 --> 00:09:07.769
I see popping up a lot, are that A Law will
betray Luffy and go for the One Piece itself,

00:09:07.769 --> 00:09:13.210
B that Law is actually a member of the secret
Marine Organization sword or C that Law will

00:09:13.210 --> 00:09:18.089
sacrifice himself to perform the immortality
surgery on Luffy. Here are my thoughts on

00:09:18.089 --> 00:09:21.410
these and why I don't think it's gonna be
either of the 3.

00:09:21.410 --> 00:09:26.870
Law could betray Luffy, based on the idea
that pirate alliances always end in betrayal,

00:09:26.870 --> 00:09:31.990
but given the fact that Law was not only freed
from his burden by Luffy, but also was prepared

00:09:31.990 --> 00:09:40.460
to die with him The point of Law's arc was
to show how kind he actually is at heart.

00:09:40.460 --> 00:09:46.329
So if Oda doesn't pull another Kanjuro, I'm
gonna say with a lot of certainty that that

00:09:46.329 --> 00:09:47.329
won't happen.

00:09:47.329 --> 00:09:51.350
The sword thing on the other hand could be
true, especially given that Corazon was a

00:09:51.350 --> 00:09:56.920
Marine spy. Drake for example has infiltrated
Kaido's crew and if Aokiji is also a member

00:09:56.920 --> 00:10:01.670
of the group, he has infiltrated Blackbeard.
Law mostly has just been traveling with his

00:10:01.670 --> 00:10:07.480
own crew and you could argue that he technically
infiltrated the straw hats. However, to be

00:10:07.480 --> 00:10:13.690
honest I don't quite see the point of it.
Law is already a fully fleshed out and interesting

00:10:13.690 --> 00:10:19.780
character. Plus he's a devoted D. Who are
the enemies of the celestial dragons. But

00:10:19.780 --> 00:10:21.120
it's possible.

00:10:21.120 --> 00:10:26.699
While I think that Law might very well die
at some point and use his ability on SOMEONE,

00:10:26.699 --> 00:10:33.439
I don't think it will be on Luffy. Luffy's
goal is to find the One Piece WITH his friends.

00:10:33.439 --> 00:10:38.500
Otherwise it's not worth it. In some way or
form, becoming pirate king is only a tool

00:10:38.500 --> 00:10:46.170
for Luffy to fulfill a bigger dream, that
doesn't include just him. So if Law sacrificed

00:10:46.170 --> 00:10:51.670
himself for him, even without Luffy's permission,
it would taint his journey. Luffy didn't want

00:10:51.670 --> 00:10:57.490
to hear what Rayleigh knew and he detests
people who use others as tools, like how Big

00:10:57.490 --> 00:11:03.189
Mom used her daughter for political alliances.
So I can imagine a scene where Law tries to

00:11:03.189 --> 00:11:08.259
sacrifice himself, but Luffy stopping him,
similarly to how he stoped Sanji and Robin

00:11:08.259 --> 00:11:33.040
form sacrificing themselves for him. Remember
that on thriller bark, Zoro, Sanji and Robin

00:11:33.040 --> 00:11:38.670
KNEW that Luffy must never know about Zoro
almost dying form his sacrifice.

00:11:38.670 --> 00:11:41.939
So Ohara, you might say now, what will Law
do then?

00:11:41.939 --> 00:11:46.339
I personally think, that law now has a new
goal and will loyalty fight side by side with

00:11:46.339 --> 00:11:51.470
Luffy till the very end. This goal is to find
the true meaning behind the D. Clan and the

00:11:51.470 --> 00:11:56.390
will of D. He has been obsessed with it his
entire life and now finally with Luffy, has

00:11:56.390 --> 00:12:01.730
found someone that actually acts in exactly
the way Corazon explained it to him. He was

00:12:01.730 --> 00:12:07.290
there, both when Luffy punched Charlos AND
when Luffy punched Doflamingo. I think Law

00:12:07.290 --> 00:12:13.230
is interested in reaching Laugh Tale, not
to become pirate king, but to learn the true

00:12:13.230 --> 00:12:16.300
history, something we see him discussing with
Robin.

00:12:16.300 --> 00:12:21.089
When you think about it, Law has the most
unsuitable crew to actually contend with most

00:12:21.089 --> 00:12:27.580
other supernova. He even send them away before
carrying out his masterplan against Dofi.

00:12:27.580 --> 00:12:32.180
His men seem to be more a crew of doctors
than of fighters, and I think that's what

00:12:32.180 --> 00:12:36.079
their role is gonna be for the rest of the
story. In other words, now that Law doesn't

00:12:36.079 --> 00:12:42.250
feel obligated to be a good D anymore, he
freely chose the goal to become one, by following

00:12:42.250 --> 00:12:54.670
the man he now believes can become pirate
king.

00:12:54.670 --> 00:12:58.980
And now we get into the spicy stuff, because
interestingly enough, Oda might have already

00:12:58.980 --> 00:13:04.899
told us what Law's role will be based on his
naming scheme. Law unties a lot of references

00:13:04.899 --> 00:13:11.180
to British sea faring. As Oda stated himself,
Law was inspired by the real-life 18th century

00:13:11.180 --> 00:13:16.759
pirate Edward Low, who was known for his cruelty,
like cutting of his enemies body parts. He

00:13:16.759 --> 00:13:22.689
had a deprived childhood surviving by stealing
and brought up by a family of criminals. Sound

00:13:22.689 --> 00:13:28.670
familiar? Oda took this real life pirate and
gave it a twist. Law is rumored to be cruel,

00:13:28.670 --> 00:13:33.860
but its actually not. Plus he cuts up people,
but only using his devil fruit ability.

00:13:33.860 --> 00:13:37.779
There are more British influences though.
The white city in the north blue where Law

00:13:37.779 --> 00:13:42.540
was born is most likely inspired by the white
city in London in northern Europe, which is

00:13:42.540 --> 00:13:48.670
famous for hosting the Japanese-British Exhibition.
Law literally sails on a yellow submarine,

00:13:48.670 --> 00:13:52.699
a homage to the famous song by the Beatles.

00:13:52.699 --> 00:13:58.149
Law's name itself though has the most clues.
In Japanese, trafalgar is actually spelled

00:13:58.149 --> 00:14:06.209
torafaruga, with luffy calling law Tora, which
literally means tiger, keeping law in line

00:14:06.209 --> 00:14:07.930
with the animal theme of the warlords.

00:14:07.930 --> 00:14:13.369
Now the other two major clues in his name
are trafalgar as well as water. In Japanese,

00:14:13.369 --> 00:14:18.769
the combination of the taboo name Water (ワーテル)
and his given name Law (ロー) forms the

00:14:18.769 --> 00:14:22.819
word&nbsp;Waterloo&nbsp;(ワーテルロー). Now,
the battle of trafalgar and the battle of

00:14:22.819 --> 00:14:28.200
Waterloo are two of the most famous battles
in history, fought in the same war that led

00:14:28.200 --> 00:14:31.110
to the downfall of emperor Napoleon.

00:14:31.110 --> 00:14:34.579
During the battle of trafalgar on the coast
of Spain, the British were led to victory

00:14:34.579 --> 00:14:40.399
by the strategy of naval hero Horario Nelson,
who not only had lost an arm, but also was

00:14:40.399 --> 00:14:45.540
shot during the battle. The battle of Waterloo
became famous as the downfall of Napoleon.

00:14:45.540 --> 00:14:50.519
In this sense, the battle of Trafalgar and
Nelsons wounds would represent Dressrosa,

00:14:50.519 --> 00:14:56.329
which is inspired by Spain. Waterloo then
would represent Wano and the end of the emperor,

00:14:56.329 --> 00:15:01.649
in this case Kaido, which was enabled by the
previous battle. Of course Law is one of the

00:15:01.649 --> 00:15:06.089
central figures fighting in Wano right now
and it will be interesting to see what will

00:15:06.089 --> 00:15:08.279
happen to him after that battle is won.

00:15:08.279 --> 00:15:13.819
There has always been a theme of death surrounding
his character. The sergeant of death, his

00:15:13.819 --> 00:15:20.180
devil fruit ability, the death number 4 in
Japanese with his 4 names and his bounty of

00:15:20.180 --> 00:15:27.589
440 million. So law might very well die, but
I would personally prefer it to see him become

00:15:27.589 --> 00:15:32.810
the happy and free person that Corazon originally
wanted him to become.

00:15:32.810 --> 00:15:36.149
